<article class="env-lemma" id="0CZ7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CZ7">Lemma <span data-tag="0CZ7">71.5.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a finite type, quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $x \in |X|$. Then $\mathcal{F}$ can be generated by $r$ elements in an étale neighbourhood of $x$ if and only if $\text{Fit}_ r(\mathcal{F})_{\overline{x}} = \mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Reduces to Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C3F" data-tag="0C3F">31.9.4</a> by étale localization (as well as the description of the local ring in Properties of Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/04KE" data-tag="04KE">66.22</a> and the fact that the strict henselization of a local ring is faithfully flat to see that the equality over the strict henselization is equivalent to the equality over the local ring). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>